/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:24:We then revisit the definition of $\gamma$-quasi-clique~\cite{pei2005mining,jiang2009mining,zeng2006coherent,liu2008effective,khalil2022parallel}.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:25:\begin{definition}[$\gamma$-quasi-clique~\cite{pei2005mining}]
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:26:    Given $H\subseteq V$ and a fraction $0\leq \gamma \leq 1$, an induced subgraph $G[H]$ is said to be a $\gamma$-quasi-clique if and only if (1) $G[H]$ is connected and (2) for any vertex $v\in H$, {\CHENG it connects at least a fraction $\gamma$ of the vertices in $H$ (excluding $v$), i.e.,} $\delta(v,H)\geq \lceil\gamma\cdot (|H|-1)\rceil$.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:29:% For a $\gamma$-quasi-clique $G[H]$, parameter $\gamma$ indicates the number of edges that each vertex at least has, i.e., $\lceil\gamma\cdot (|H|-1)\rceil$, which is proportional to the size of $H$. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:31:% when $\gamma=1$, 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:33:Besides, $\gamma$-quasi-clique has the following {\cheng two} properties. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:37:    For a $\gamma$-quasi-clique $G[H]$, a subgraph of $G[H]$ might not be a $\gamma$-quasi-clique. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:45:    For $\gamma\geq 0.5$, the diameter of a $\gamma$-quasi-clique is at most 2. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:49:% In this paper, we only focus on those $\gamma$-quasi-cliques with $\gamma\geq 0.5$. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:50:{\cheng Following~\cite{pei2005mining}, we focus on those $\gamma$-quasi-cliques with $\gamma\geq 0.5$ only in this paper.}
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:51:This is because for a smaller value of $\gamma$, there exist numerous $\gamma$-quasi-cliques yet the majority of them are of small size and not cohesive~\cite{khalil2022parallel,guo2020scalable,pei2005mining}.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:54:% to further reduce the large number of $\gamma$-quasi-cliques, 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:55:prior studies~\cite{zeng2006coherent,liu2008effective,guo2020scalable,khalil2022parallel} often {\cheng focus on} a compact representation of the set of $\gamma$-quasi-cliques, namely the set of \emph{maximal} $\gamma$-quasi-cliques.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:57:\begin{definition}[Maximal $\gamma$-quasi-clique]
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:58:    A $\gamma$-quasi-clique $G[H]$ is said to be maximal if and only if there is no other $\gamma$-quasi-clique $G[H']$ containing $G[H]$, i.e., $H\subseteq H'$.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:61:In this paper, we use QC (resp. MQC) as a shorthand of $\gamma$-quasi-clique (resp. maximal $\gamma$-quasi-clique) when the context is clear. Following~\cite{pei2005mining,liu2008effective,guo2020scalable,khalil2022parallel}, we consider a size threshold $\theta$ {\cheng for} each MQC $G[H]$ to be enumerated, namely $|H|\geq \theta$, since small MQCs are numerous and not statistically significant for real applications~\cite{khalil2022parallel,guo2020scalable,pei2005mining}.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:67:\begin{problem}[Maximal $\gamma$-quasi-clique Enumeration~\cite{pei2005mining,liu2008effective,guo2020scalable,khalil2022parallel}]
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:69:    Given a graph $G=(V,E)$, a fraction threshold $\gamma\in [0.5, 1]$ and a positive integer size threshold $\theta$, the Maximal $\gamma$-Quasi-Clique Enumeration ({\cheng MQCE}) Problem aims to find all MQCs $G[H]$ {\cheng with} $|H|\geq \theta$.
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:72:\noindent\textbf{NP-hardness.} The MQCE problem is NP-hard since the optimization problem {\cheng of} finding the MQC with the largest number of vertices is NP-hard~\cite{pastukhov2018maximum}. %
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:75:{\CHENG Furthermore, } determining whether a QC is maximal is NP-hard~\cite{sanei2018enumerating}. 
/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/problem.tex:76:{\CHENG In contrast, } determining if {\CHENG a structure that satisfies the hereditary property}, e.g., a clique~\cite{bron1973algorithm}, is maximal can usually be done in polynomial.
