/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.34Gdm0/src/framework5.tex:1076:%\noindent\textbf{T2: Maximality checking.} \texttt{FastQC} would also inevitably output some non-maximal $\gamma$-QCs and needs to monitors whether a sub-branch of the current one would find a $\gamma$-QC (line 21-25), similar as \texttt{Quick+}. Those non-maximal outputs would be temporally stored and then be filtered out by a post-processing procedure, which consumes some resources. However, the problem of checking maximality of a $\gamma$-QC directly is NP-hard~\cite{sanei2018enumerating}. To mitigate this issue, we observe that for a MQC $G[H]$, there does not exist a vertex $v$ outside $H$ such that $G[H\cup \{v\}]$ is also a QC (i.e., $\Delta(H\cup \{v\})\leq \tau(|H|+1)$ based on Lemma~\ref{lemma:TD_Property2}). Clearly, it can be checked in polynomial time. Hence, we output QCs only if this maximality condition is satisfied (line 9 and line 22), which will help to reduce non-maximal outputs.
