index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..70164fd359ccb27e8145df2e270873b69da08f35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+# Large induced quasi-cliques from arXiv:2305.14047
+
+> **Status:** the generator passes every local gate, but this directory is not
+> submission-ready. The required OpenRouter run aborted because the configured
+> key has exhausted its total limit. The script-written error transcripts are
+> retained; no oracle error is counted as a failed solve.
+
+## Profile
+
+| field | value |
+|---|---|
+| track | **A — structural hardness** |
+| native domain | combinatorics |
+| object regime | finite discrete |
+| computational core | graph |
+| certificate form | integer tuple |
+| intuition | constraint propagation through the disconnection/complement view |
+| domain essentiality | native |
+| reduction | none |
+
+## Problem and provenance
+
+The source is Yu and Long, [*Fast Maximal Quasi-clique Enumeration: A
+Pruning and Branching Co-Design Approach*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14047).
+A solver receives an undirected graph and must return exactly 21 vertices whose
+induced subgraph is connected and has minimum degree 18. This is precisely a
+`9/10`-quasi-clique under Definition 1 in Section 2.1. Checking a witness only
+requires exact adjacency counts and a connectivity traversal.
+
+The answer is known by inverse generation. The generator first samples 21
+uniform vertex labels, then makes their induced graph `K_21` with one randomly
+ordered Hamiltonian cycle deleted. Every planted vertex therefore has degree
+18. Only afterward are background edges sampled. The cross-edge probability is
+chosen so that planted and background vertices have the same expected total
+degree, suppressing the simplest planting signature.
+
+This deliberately does **not** claim to certify maximality. Section 2.1 says
+exact maximality checking is NP-hard, and Section 4.5 calls the test “no single
+outside vertex extends the set” only a *necessary* condition. Because
+quasi-cliques are non-hereditary, that test is not an exact maximality witness.
+The family instead asks for one paper-native large quasi-clique, not the full
+MQCE enumeration output.
+
+## Why Track A
+
+Section 2.1 establishes NP-hardness of MQCE, while Theorem 1 bounds FastQC by
+`O(n d alpha_k^n)` with `alpha_k < 2`. At shipping parameters `n=384`,
+`gamma=0.9`, and `theta=21`, the paper's `tau(n)` parameter is 39, so the stated
+base is already close to 2. Section 6 also reports that denser graphs weaken
+degree pruning and raise running time. These results motivate—but do not prove
+hardness of—this generated distribution. The distributional evidence is the
+measured panel: six attacks each failed on 8/8 seeds, including centered
+spectral recovery, a construction-aware complement-cycle hill climb, and an
+exact fixed-deficiency branch-and-bound search capped at 250,000 nodes. The
+last attack consumed a median 250,011 visited calls and 2.638 seconds.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+The hand-scale preset is `make_instance(n=12, k=5, seed=0)`, with `gamma=1/2`:
+
+```text
+0: 1 2 4 5 6 10
+1: 0 2 3 6 7 8 9
+2: 0 1 3 4 6 8 9 11
+3: 1 2 4 7 8
+4: 0 2 3 5 7 8 9
+5: 0 4 9 11
+6: 0 1 2 8 11
+7: 1 3 4 9 11
+8: 1 2 3 4 6 11
+9: 1 2 4 5 7 10 11
+10: 0 9 11
+11: 2 5 6 7 8 9 10
+```
+
+Its planted answer is `<answer>0, 4, 6, 7, 11</answer>`.
+`verify(inst, inst["answer"])` returns `(True, "ok")`; dropping vertex 11
+returns `(False, "wrong size: expected 5 vertices, got 4")`. A person can solve
+this setting on paper: only 792 five-subsets exist, and 245 are valid. The demo
+illustrates the definition rather than hardness.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| preset | n | witness size | gamma | candidate-space bits | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 12 | 5 | 1/2 | 10 | hand example; hardener skips it |
+| **easy** | **384** | **21** | **9/10** | **115** | provisional shipping preset; local gates pass |
+| medium | 512 | 21 | 9/10 | 123 | available escalation |
+| hard | 768 | 21 | 9/10 | 136 | available escalation and G7 doubled size |
+
+No preset has a valid oracle verdict yet; `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY="easy"` is
+therefore provisional rather than evidence-backed.
+
+## Local gate results
+
+| gate | measured result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 12/12 plants verify; 12/12 answers survive JSON round-trip |
+| G2 | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | tagged prose round-trips; garbage returns `None` |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 uniform exact-size guesses; space = 20,929,752,116,090,168,002,042,327,985,942,400 |
+| G5 | demo exact count 245; shipping B&B median 250,011 calls / 2.638 s |
+| G6 | six attacks, each 0/8 successes |
+| G7 | doubled `n=768` instance builds, verifies, and has a larger space |
+| G8 | 80/80 key invariance checks, 80/80 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | 80 chars, 21 atoms, about 20 tokens, 273 intended exact operations |
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+The bare harness made four redraws at the easy preset. Every call returned HTTP
+403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`, so `harden.py` aborted without a
+verdict. Those four script-owned records remain in
+`llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`.
+
+| arm | scored solves / attempts | retained records | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| bare | unavailable / 0 | 4 API errors | no hardness claim possible |
+| structural hint | unavailable / 0 | 4 API errors | diagnostic not run |
+| placebo hint | unavailable / 0 | 4 API errors | diagnostic not run |
+
+Hinted-minus-placebo is unavailable, not zero evidence. A funded key must rerun
+all three arms in separate directories before submission.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import gen_2305_14047 as g
+
+params = g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **params)
+statement = g.render(inst)
+raw = "<answer>" + ", ".join(map(str, inst["answer"])) + "</answer>"
+answer = g.parse_answer(raw)
+assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After regenerating valid bare and G9 oracle evidence, emit from the repository
+root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 2305.14047
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The paper proves worst-case hardness, not hardness of this inverse-generated
+distribution; the attack results are empirical calibration only. The exact
+branch-and-bound attack is budgeted, so failure means “not within 250,000
+nodes,” not an impossibility result. The 0/200,000 density result is for uniform
+21-subsets and neither counts all solutions nor supplies a statistical upper
+bound below `1e-6`. A solver with a better k-plex/MQC implementation, an ILP or
+SDP relaxation, or more aggressive local search may still break the family;
+full FastQC, Quick+, ILP, and SDP implementations were not run. Finally, the
+four-round 1-WL key is an isomorphism invariant, not a complete graph
+isomorphism canonical form. These uncertainties are exactly why valid
+four-vendor transcripts remain mandatory.
