Built the verified generator, but final oracle validation is blocked by an exhausted OpenRouter key.

- [gen_2305_14047.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/gen_2305_14047.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The full-text audit corrected the proposed family: the paper says single-vertex non-extendability is only necessary for maximality, while exact maximality checking is NP-hard. The module therefore asks for one exact-size, paper-native induced γ-quasi-clique rather than using an invalid maximality checker. [Paper full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2305.14047v2)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Structured guesses: 0/200,000.
- Six attacks: 0/8 each.
- Exact branch-and-bound baseline: median 250,011 calls and 2.638 seconds.
- Canonical-key tests: 80/80 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.
- Answer: 80 characters, 21 elements; intended route 273 operations.

All three oracle runs aborted with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. Their authentic error transcripts were retained, but they provide no hardness verdict. Consequently, `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY="easy"` remains provisional and the directory is not submission-ready until those runs are repeated with a funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
