236:Intuitively, Type I pruning rules are conducted on $C$ and aim to refine $C$ by removing those vertices that satisfy certain conditions; Type II pruning rules are conducted on $S$ and aim to prune those branches where vertices in $S$ satisfy certain conditions. 
