     9	{\cheng Specifically, \texttt{Quick+}} recursively partitions the search space (i.e., the set of possible vertex sets) to multiple sub-spaces via \emph{branching}. Each sub-space, {\cheng which corresponds to} a \emph{branch}, is represented by a triple of three vertex sets $(S,C,D)$ {\cheng explained} as follows. 
