codex
One important audit remains before I trust the official-code timeout: DCFastQC is an enumerator, so “did not finish” is not the same as “did not find one witness.” I’m rerunning it with output enabled and will inspect whether it emits any quasi-clique before the timeout; if it does, the family fails the standard-algorithm attack despite the long completion time.
