codex
The draft now records the paper’s easy regimes explicitly: larger `γ` and `θ` improve pruning, while sparse low-degeneracy graphs benefit from divide-and-conquer. The generated instances deliberately counter only the latter by using dense degree-balanced graphs; this is empirical distributional hardness, not a theorem-derived guarantee, and the README will say so.
