The exact definition already changes the proposed verifier materially: maximality is not “no single outside vertex can be added.” Quasi-cliques are non-hereditary, and the paper states that deciding whether any larger quasi-clique contains a given one is NP-hard. A plain vertex-set answer therefore is not cheaply verifiable as maximal; I’m now checking the paper’s decomposition and bounds for a certificate or a different native search task.
