/tmp/arxiv2305.14047.tNm2tP/framework5.tex:170:% Consider a branch $B=(S,C,D)$ and all of partial sets $S_i$ in the search space corresponding to this branch (i.e., all possible $S_i$ such that $S\subseteq S_i\subseteq S\cup C$). It is NP-hard to determine whether branch $B$ holds a QC (or formally, whether one of the partial sets inside induces a QC) due to the exponential number of partial sets (the proof is put {\cheng in the technical report~\cite{TR}} for simplicity). Consequently, \texttt{Quick+} needs to explore $O(2^{n})$ branches {\cheng in the worse case}.
