codex
I found a viable native Track B route in the paper’s own branch-and-bound setting, without pretending maximality is locally checkable in general: use the paper’s allowed `γ=1` case, where a quasi-clique is a clique and maximality is executable, and present a succinct Cayley graph whose affine-line certificate is verified exactly. Generic line search has millions of candidates; the compact route is recognizing a shared polynomial root in the graph’s linear forms. I’m replacing the earlier random-plant build with this bounded matrix certificate and will measure both routes.
