The measured Track B gap is now explicit: the successful mechanical enumeration takes a median 6,740,125 exact field operations (0.219 s in Python), while the polynomial-root invariant needs a median 108 operations, 150 worst observed. I’m running the two G9 diagnostic arms in isolated copies; the same exhausted API key is expected to leave them as honest error-only records, not scored attempts.
