A final certificate-cost audit found an important issue before handoff: the initially measured “mechanical” route was not the strongest obvious algorithm—the displayed constraints also admit Gaussian elimination. I’m correcting the shipping regime so the disclosed standard algorithm is the actual one, with a measured five-figure exact-operation cost, while the common-root route stays below the 300-operation cap. This is necessary for an honest Track B claim.
