codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator for [arXiv:2305.14047](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14047):

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/gen_2305_14047.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2305.14047/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Key results:

- All local G1–G9 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guesses: 0/200,000; exact success probability `3.1691e-67`.
- Five attacks: each 0/8.
- Honest reference algorithm: modular Gaussian elimination, 495,207 median field operations.
- Compact route: 209 median operations, 215 worst case.
- Shipping answer: 389 characters, 192 atoms, approximately 98 tokens.
- Exact small-graph exhaustions confirmed symmetry, regularity, clique maximality, and uniqueness of the valid direction.

The original proposed random planted quasi-clique construction was discarded because the paper explicitly says single-vertex extension is insufficient to certify maximality for general quasi-cliques. The replacement uses the paper’s exact `gamma=1` boundary with a construction-backed maximality certificate.

One external blocker remains: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “total limit exceeded” on every bare, hinted, and placebo redraw. Consequently, no oracle calls were scored and no `hardened` verdict can honestly be claimed yet. The script-generated error records are preserved; the result is locally complete but not submission-ready until the oracle loop is rerun with a funded key.
